# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 3: a bare `Counter` in a unit-level method's body executes the
# named Structure natively -- the pair (its code node, Counter) through lmx_call_prim, whose walk hook
# is the root's executor.  bump executes it twice and reads Counter\n: 1, the declaration ran again.
# The root wrote 5 before the call and reads 1 after it: the last state stays in the field.  Was
# unit_named_struct_exec_method_refused.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 1U
return
fn: bump () size_t
    Counter
    Counter
    size_t: v 9U
    v: Counter\n
return: v
size_t: before 9U
before: Counter\n
Counter\n: 5U
size_t: got 9U
got: bump()
size_t: after 9U
after: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: before = 0U && got = 1U && after = 1U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
